FROM qwen3:4b-instruct

# Tuned for coding-agent use (Qwen Code / large tool+file context per turn).
#
# Built on the "instruct" (non-thinking) tag rather than the default hybrid
# qwen3:4b: testing showed the hybrid model ignores the API's think:false
# flag and rambles through open-ended reasoning text regardless, so a real
# non-thinking checkpoint is the fix, not a request-time toggle.
#
# num_ctx: default 4096 is far too small for agent prompts — Qwen Code's own
# system prompt + tool schemas alone measured at 28,422 tokens in testing,
# before any conversation/file content is added. Too-small context makes
# llama.cpp's --context-shift silently drop the original instruction
# mid-turn, which is what caused runaway/rambling generations during
# testing. The real prompt size isn't fixed — it varied 28.4k/29.8k/33.4k
# tokens across test runs (interactive mode reads extra context files like
# ~/.qwen/output-language.md on top of the base tool schema) — so 32768 was
# too tight and got hit live. 40960 gives real headroom above the observed
# ~33.4k peak; 65536 pushed resident memory to 12GB and spilled off-GPU on
# this 16GB machine, so avoid going that high.
PARAMETER num_ctx 40960
# Hard ceiling per turn so a bad generation stops in seconds, not minutes.
PARAMETER num_predict 800
# Base model ships with repeat_penalty 1 (disabled), which makes
# degenerate/looping output more likely.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
